{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19048-2nd-generation-pantheons","id":19048,"title":"2nd Generation Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-27T01:58:13-08:00","id":19048,"title":"2nd Generation Pantheons","content":"The premise is this: the Gods have not been keeping on the sidelines during the past couple hundreds/ thousands of years. Instead, our world and the worlds of myth continued to be inextricably linked. Not only that, but what happens on earth is mirrored in the Godrealms. When a people falls, so does their pantheon. When a culture becomes dominant, so do their gods. While this is evident in history books with stories of gods and men interacting up to the present day, it is most obvious in the effects on the pantheons themselves.<br /> <br /> The Challenge: pick a moment in history, such as the European contact with the Americas, Portuguese dominance in the Indian Ocean, the War of the Roses, etc. Trace out corresponding effects on the most closely associated pantheons. This is assuming that despite the intervention of the gods, history pretty much remained the same, with one major exception: Monotheistic religions never gained ground. Those cultures still rose to prominence, but under the auspices of their more polytheistic heritage. <br /> <br /> This could include the death of old gods or the apotheosis of Scions. Some may have become new Titan Avatars. Pantheons could mix as their patron cultures migrated and changed. Entire new pantheons would have emerged.<br /> <br /> I'm excited to see what can be imagined","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/911-phoebuslore","name":"phoebuslore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar911_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T09:26:24-08:00","id":19222,"title":"","content":"You mean like the Dodekatheon getting a resurgence of power during the eighth to eleventh centuries as the works of the Greek and Roman World get retranslated and brought back, while still being predominantly under the thumb of the Arabic pantheon/monodominant? Or the GrecoAesir Alliance taking full advantage of the Opium Wars in order to gain access to coastal cities and, at least for Zeus, more beautiful women? I can almost see the Shen in an uproar about the first time a Scion of Zeus starts acting up in Shanghai or Beijing.<br /> <br /> Or suppose it's more like the Chinese immigaration to the western coast of America, appealing to the Shen for aid and guidance, only to fall on deaf ears as the Celestial Bureaucracy is still 'we do not recognize anywhere but China as real', and the Mannitou and Aztlanti seizing the opportunity. This then leads to all sorts of conflicts, as the few Shen paying attention in the US must now deal with ambitious native gods, the racial tensions of the Irish/Tuatha and African/Loa in competing for jobs/Spheres of Influence, and even the few odd things like robber barons working immigrant populations to death laying tracks and blowing up mountains in order to gain access to artifacts, passage into the Underworld, or even just gathering Massive Quantities of Itztli.<br /> <br /> Why is it so easy to see the transAmerican railway as a giant blood sacrifice?<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you don't use the Yankee pantheon, the whole premise of 'melting pot countries' like Chile, Bolivia, Brazil, and the US just becomes this massive cacophony of powerplays between the Old World Pantheons, and the Aztlanti/Apu/other populations trying to stay relevant. Tlaloc working with industry leaders to keep child labor in place. The neoClassical architecture of the White House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T16:13:23-08:00","id":21345,"title":"","content":"Exactly like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/911-phoebuslore","name":"phoebuslore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar911_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:11:09-08:00","id":21743,"title":"","content":"Or with the imminent invasion from foreign pantheons from Europe, China and Japan, the innumerable gods of the northern native Americans, team up with the varied (more than people know) pantheons of central and south America to expel the intruders and safeguard their lands and people. An alliance like that would last as long as there was a big enough threat, and might force all settlers to negotiate in a totally different way than history has shown. Imagine the modern Americas formed on the terms of the peoples indigenous to the area as opposed to the invaders!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:26:17-08:00","id":21786,"title":"","content":"The might and terror of the Yuan Dynasty, as the Mongolians' acquiring of the Middle Kingdom is mirrored in Heaven, the Shen now bowing to the Blue Wolf and Feral Doe.<br /> <br /> The Devas' initial reaction to the Buddha, and the Chinese and Japanese pantheons initially reacting to Buddhist monks as foreign incursions or subversive elements to their hegemony. Their dealings with this new philosophy and its effects on their followers and Overworld are then applied, in small part, to the oncoming of the Jesuits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T14:12:13-08:00","id":25339,"title":"","content":"Two of the strongest influences on the creation of the American governmental system were Athens and the Iroquois Confederation. Assuming that monotheism never took hold, perhaps a council containing members of the Dodekatheon and the great spirits of the Iroquois came into existence during that time period, and rose to dominance after WW2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T16:11:21-08:00","id":25414,"title":"","content":"Hellenism Ascendant! Assuming only a few relatively minor changes, the world becomes a very different place indeed. If Alexander survives even just a little bit longer (perhaps with the help of Zeus, or perhaps the Pesedjet; maybe both!) he might go on to conquer Arabia and the Western Mediterranean, perhaps even making incursions into sub-Saharan Africa. Even if his empire shatters amongst the Diadochi as it did in real life, stronger Hellenic states might still emerge. Pyrrus (an unfortunate Scion of Ares? Or Athena?) might form an alliance with the Carthaginians, or Mithridates VI (an interesting character, and a good candidate for being a Scion too; perhaps of Mithras or Bahram, but Zeus works too) might route the Romans in Asia Minor, or Marcus Antonius might defeat Octavian and preserve the Ptolemaic line (the Pesedjet again). Whatever the case, Rome never rises, and a vibrant new era of Hellenistic culture spreads from the Pillars of Hercules to the Indus Valley.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the Dodekatheon ride high on their success. Greek language, art, architecture and theatre thrive, and pagan philosophers and mystery cults manage to co-opt any nascent monotheistic groups. The Scions of Zeus, Hades, Poseidon, Aphrodite, Ares, Dionysus, Artemis, Athena and the rest party, drink, fight and generally have adventures across the Mediterranean, Near East and beyond. But this also brings the Dodekatheon into closer contact with other Pantheons, for good or for ill. Following Alexander's declaration of godhood by the oracle of Siwa, and the fascination with all things Egyptian, the once insular Pesedjet spread their influence across the Middle East and Mediterranean. Isis in particular enjoys widespread appeal. Their rivals the Yazata have not done so well, re-building their power base in Seleucid Persia as native Greco-Persian dynasties rise and fall. Further east, the Devas are much as they always have been, but the spread of Buddhism has allowed them to move even further east, into the mandala states of Southeast Asia... and west, into the Greco-Buddhist kingdoms of Bactria. Soon Scions of Shiva, Vishnu, Kali, Surya, Ganesha and the other Indian gods are turning up in Alexandria, Sinope, Rhodes, Cheronesus, Ctesiphon, Babylon, Syracuse, Tyre, and even Athens!<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, on the far fringes of Europe and Africa, the Tuatha and the forebearers of the Loa remain exotic and mysterious. They have encounters with the Dodekatheon and their Greek (and Hellenized) followers but they are a mixed bag. It is too early to make anything of them one way or another. The Babylonian Pantheon never falls either. Its still around and kicking, as are the related Phoenician, Assyrian and other Near Eastern Pantheons (though they cannot rival the majesty of the Dodekatheon and their Egyptian and Indian allies, of course). And beyond the Pillars of Hercules? Who can say...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","name":"Zakariya Ali Sher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T08:21:20-08:00","id":28741,"title":"","content":"Britain (or should I say, Britainnia) is a three-way slugfest between the presence of the Theoi/Roman influence, the Aesir, and the Tuatha. Canonically, the Tuatha slowly begin to be pushed into Scotland, Wales, and eventually into Ireland along, while the Aesir seem to seize control of England, pushing the Theoi out and the Tuatha westward. But That Could Have Gone any number of ways.<br /> <br /> Another thing I seem to notice is that, whenever I see a thread about monotheism in Scion, it revolves around Christianity or Atenism. How did the Yazata, Pesedjet, Deva, and Celestial Bureaucracy react to, say, Islam? The spread of Islam did not affect these faiths as much as, say, Christianity did on the practice of the Greek, Aesir, Egyptian, and Irish faiths. Might this be a example of the differing Pantheon Virtues and philosophies, the population's faith or cultures? Could the above-mentioned pantheons be using Islam in some fashion, for cross-pantheon communication or trade (with travelling Scions masquerading as wandering scholars or priests of Islam in order to act in regions normally under a different pantheon's control), or is that more something Buddhism would be used for?<br /> Would a Deva-born Scion be more prone to using the guise of a sheik, or a monk, as a disguise in the first and second millenia, in order to acquire some artifact in China?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:39:15-08:00","id":28938,"title":"","content":"Since it talks about 2nd gen pantheons, I keep thinking about how the Teen Titans was formed in the DC Universe because they believed that adults weren't giving teens the respect they deserve. Perhaps Onyx Path can add in some fledgling pantheons that came to be in certain points of history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T15:33:49-08:00","id":28965,"title":"","content":"I think Australia would probably become a cultural melting pot for all those Gods who didn't quite fit in with their natural Pantheon, or decided they needed to change as the world changed (A very rare idea indeed). Australia is probably considered the back-woods of the Gods. The other Gods there are incredibly powerful, but they're all asleep or hiding - too scared to come out for fear of death, but otherwise it's free for the taking.<br /> <br /> The Aesir and Tuatha came in to check it out and a few decided to set up shop. Then over the years others have come in casually to check out this large chunk of land and some decided to stay. There's probably a few running around that have formed a loose alliance, but haven't taken it the step further to call it a Pantheon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/735-hitashippo","name":"HitAShippo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T16:36:46-08:00","id":28996,"title":"","content":"I think the Rainbow Serpent (name varies from tribe I believe), might have something to say about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T17:56:02-08:00","id":29035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zakariya Ali Sher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/19048-2nd-generation-pantheons?p=25414#post25414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, on the far fringes of Europe and Africa, the Tuatha and the forebearers of the Loa remain exotic and mysterious. They have encounters with the Dodekatheon and their Greek (and Hellenized) followers but they are a mixed bag. It is too early to make anything of them one way or another. The Babylonian Pantheon never falls either. Its still around and kicking, as are the related Phoenician, Assyrian and other Near Eastern Pantheons (though they cannot rival the majesty of the Dodekatheon and their Egyptian and Indian allies, of course). And beyond the Pillars of Hercules? Who can say...</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, though, if we're going by real-world demographics, there are potentially <i>millions</i> of Vodoo and African Diasporic Religion practitioners active today. I think that the Loa have more of a hand in things in America (north and South, let's not forget Santeiria and Cambodle) than people would","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:06:44-08:00","id":29084,"title":"","content":"<b>The Middle Kingdom Beset By Barbarians (Mid 19th Century to Beginning of 20th)</b><br /> <br /> The Celestial Bureaucracy had a particularly rough time during this period. Western imperialism (and later the influence of a modernizing Japan) in the World sought opportunities as the Qing Dynasty was facing the Heavenly Signs of natural disasters and economic turmoil... then the British smashed open the floodgates with the First Opium War. The Qing military was completely behind in technology, and suffered catastrophic defeat.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Manchus that dominated the dynastic power structure were foreign and hated by the population. The Amatsukami, Dodekathon, Aesir, Atzlanti and other Pantheons likewise seized the opportunity to extend their influence upon the borders of Tian, pressuring the Bureaucracy for concessions on all sides. The shen were more able to rebuff the foreign gods, but were heavily riven in disputes as to how to respond.<br /> <br /> The situation was set for Hundun to light the spark, which the Elder Chaos did very well. The avatar Chiyou took on the cover of Hong Xiuquan, a failed civil service candidate who claimed to have visions of Heaven and the true lord of the cosmos (his lesser brother indeed), igniting what history records as the Taiping Rebellion. The massive following and armies behind the rebellion crushed government forces, bolstered by black calamities and chaos hounds. Likewise, other shen were tempted into service of Hundun and proceeded to wreak havoc in Tian. Naturally, other titanspawn flocked to the strife to make matters worse.<br /> <br /> Both World and Overworld of the Middle Kingdom suffered horrendously, Chiyou letting his role of Hong fall into the background and the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom sabotage itself through corruption, British and French soldiers giving the Qing the edge at last.<br /> <br /> The Celestial Bureaucracy was not saved from the fallen W\u01d4 Ti\u011b M\u00e9n (Five Iron Gates - a dissatisfied minor god of military command), <div align=\"left\">Y\u0101nw\u00f9 B\u00ecng (Ill Smoke - the disreputable shen assigned to the purviews of opium) and R\u00f3uru\u01cen Des\u012bch\u00f3u F\u016br\u00e9n (Soft Lady Silk - under abuse by a higher ranking male shen) by their own efforts, but by the combined efforts of Thor, Apollo, Ares, Vidar, Susan-oo, Set and Sobek.<br /> <br /> The extreme debt that the diminished Celestial Bureaucracy were forced to acknowledge (bound by Fate) crippled the pantheon to the level of a third-rate power, and not until the most recent years of Guan Yu's term as the Jade Emperor has any sign of recovery appeared.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1654-the_gm","name":"The_GM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}